index 0e61cd46d9eef7bd98130ca8ba05c558833e4741..6ac6e406d2bb0c7407be6fa66c16e099fd28557a 100644
--- a/docs/python-api.rst
+++ b/docs/python-api.rst
@@ -353,6 +353,8 @@ Raw SQL writes with db.execute()
 
 Write statements executed with :ref:`db.execute() <python_api_execute>` follow the same rule as everything else: they are committed automatically as soon as they have run.
 
+If a write fails outside an explicit transaction, any implicit transaction opened by that statement is rolled back before the error is raised. If a transaction is already open, the error is raised without rolling back that transaction, so earlier work is preserved and the caller can continue using, commit or roll back the transaction.
+
 .. code-block:: python
 
     db.execute("insert into news (headline) values (?)", ["Dog wins award"])
